        "narrative_kicker": "Our Story",
        "narrative_lead": "Technology has changed dramatically since EZQuest was founded in 1994. We\u2019ve witnessed the evolution from SCSI to USB, FireWire, Thunderbolt, USB-C, USB4, and beyond. Through every generation of innovation, one thing has remained unchanged: our commitment to designing products that solve real problems for real people.",
        "narrative_body": "<p>EZQuest began with a simple belief that great products don\u2019t start with engineering drawings. <strong>They start by listening.</strong></p><p>Founder Ebrahim Zmehrir, an electronics engineer with a lifelong passion for designing and building technology, established EZQuest with a vision of making computer connectivity easier, more reliable, and more intuitive.</p><p>As technology evolved, so did EZQuest. During the transition from analog to digital video editing, EZQuest became one of the pioneers in FireWire storage solutions. Our products were showcased by Apple at Macworld San Francisco.</p><p>Today, our focus is on USB-C and Thunderbolt connectivity solutions, including hubs, docking stations, adapters, cables, and power solutions that simplify everyday technology. While our products have evolved, our philosophy has not.</p><p>Every EZQuest product begins with customer feedback. We don\u2019t design products based on assumptions or trends. We listen to professionals, creators, businesses, educators, and everyday users to understand their challenges before creating solutions.</p><p>We have never believed in creating \u201cme-too\u201d products. If a product already exists, our question isn\u2019t, \u201cCan we make one too?\u201d It\u2019s, \u201cHow can we make it better?\u201d</p><p>Perhaps the greatest compliment we receive isn\u2019t an award, it\u2019s hearing from customers who are still using products they purchased decades ago.</p>",
        "closer_line1": "Our goal has never been to earn a sale.",
        "closer_line2_pre": "Our goal is to",
        "closer_accent": "earn a fan.",
        "closer_sub": "One customer at a time.",
